{
  "language": "en",
  "wordOrder": "verb-first",
  "purpose": "English has no capital letters that mark nouns and no closed list holds every verb, so M01 flags a task name only on evidence of a wrong form: one word; no word with a letter after the first, or only placeholder letters (Step 3, Path A); a label prefix (SAP:); a first word from nonVerbStarters or nounStarters; a gerund (Checking invoice); or, after a first word that is no verb, a last word that is a participle, a state word, a listed verb or a noun made from one (Invoice checked, Invoice check, Invoice approval). A first word that is a listed verb, a prefix plus a listed verb (reorder, pre approve), a verb phrase (back up) or has a verb suffix (-ate, -ize, -ise, -ify) needs an object after it; two words of a homograph and a state (Order shipped) are flagged. Any other first word passes and is named in hint H14, so a shorter verb list gives more hints, not more findings. Events (M06) and messages (M05) are flagged when they start with a listed verb outside nounVerbHomographs; an event whose last word is a participle or a state word is not flagged, nor a message whose last word is a message noun after a verb that does not send it (Deploy request; Send invoice is flagged). A container is flagged when it is one listed verb or ends in a participle. Extend or trim the lists with a BPMN_NAMING overlay; it accepts only the lists of its schema (here verbs, verbPhrases, nounVerbHomographs, stateWords, nounStarters, messageNouns).",
  "listNotes": {
    "questionMarks": "M02 reads it: a gateway name counts as a question when it contains one of these strings.",
    "verbs": "M01 passes a task name that starts with a listed verb; an unlisted first word without evidence against it passes with hint H14. M06 and M05 flag an event or message that starts with a listed word outside nounVerbHomographs; M01 flags a container that is one listed word.",
    "verbPhrases": "Multi-word verbs (back up, shut down, hand off) that may open a task name; at least one more word must follow.",
    "verbPrefixes": "Prefixes (re, pre, co) that may come before a listed verb, joined (reorder) or as a word of their own (pre approve); a joined prefix needs at least three more letters.",
    "infinitiveSuffixes": "A first word with one of these endings and the minimum length (calibrate, optimize, centralise, simplify), less the exceptions of the ending (certificate, template), counts as a task verb without a list entry.",
    "nounVerbHomographs": "Listed verbs that are also nouns (order, request): M06 and M05 do not flag an event or message that starts with one, so \"Request for details\" passes; M01 flags a task name of one and a participle or state word (Order shipped).",
    "participles": "The -ed ending plus irregular forms (sent, written), less the exceptions (need, feed): M01 flags a container, a task name whose first word is no verb and M05 a message whose last word is one; M06 does not flag an event that starts with a verb but ends in one.",
    "stateWords": "State words (open, ready, complete): M06 does not flag an event that starts with a verb when its last word is one; M01 flags a task name whose first word is no verb and whose last word is one (Payment due).",
    "nonVerbStarters": "Determiners, pronouns, prepositions, conjunctions and auxiliaries (the, our, for, and, is): M01 flags a task name that starts with one. A closed class, so the overlay does not change it.",
    "nounStarters": "Frequent nouns and adjectives that never open an instruction (customer, system, final): M01 flags a task name that starts with one, unless the word is also on the verb list.",
    "messageNouns": "Nouns that name a message (request, order, invoice): M05 does not flag a message flow whose last word is one for starting with a verb (Deploy request), unless that verb is on sendVerbs; a participle at the end is still flagged.",
    "sendVerbs": "Verbs whose object is the message itself (send, submit, forward): M05 flags \"Send invoice\" although invoice is a message noun.",
    "eventMarkers": "Read by the marker inference for events (message, timer, error, signal, escalation, conditional), not by M01, M05 or M06; a keyword matches a whole word only."
  },
